# OrderFlow sample requests. Open in Visual Studio 2026 or VS Code with the REST Client extension and run them top to bottom.
# Prerequisites: the API and Worker are running, and scripts/seed-dev.ps1 has created the demo accounts and products.
# The demo password belongs to the local seed accounts only.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:53375/api/v1
@password = OrderFlow-Demo-2026!

### 1. Browse the catalog anonymously (served through the Redis cache-aside path)
# @name products
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?search=lamp&isAvailable=true&sort=price&page=1&pageSize=5

### 2. Product detail. The first read is a cache miss, the next one a hit (watch orderflow.cache.hits)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/{{products.response.body.$.items[0].id}}

### 3. Sign in as the customer. API clients get both tokens in JSON; the web client asks for the refresh cookie instead
# @name customer
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "customer@orderflow.example", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 4. Put one unit in the cart
# @name cart
POST {{baseUrl}}/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": "{{products.response.body.$.items[0].id}}", "quantity": 1 }

### 5. Shipping methods offered at checkout
# @name shipping
GET {{baseUrl}}/shipping-methods

### 6. Checkout. Returns 202 with a PendingInventory order; the Worker does the rest.
# Use a new key for each new order. Send it twice with the same key: the second answer is the stored first one, and no second order is created (AC-02).
# Change the body but keep the key: 409 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED.
# @name order
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: sample-checkout-0001
X-Correlation-Id: sample-trace-0001

{
  "cartId": "{{cart.response.body.$.id}}",
  "shippingMethodId": "{{shipping.response.body.$[0].id}}",
  "paymentMethod": "CardSimulation",
  "couponCode": null,
  "deliveryAddress": {
    "recipientName": "Demo Customer",
    "phone": "0900000000",
    "line1": "1 Demo Street",
    "ward": "Ward 1",
    "district": "District 1",
    "province": "Ho Chi Minh City",
    "countryCode": "VN"
  }
}

### 7. Follow the order: PendingInventory -> AwaitingPayment -> Paid -> Processing, with its status history
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{order.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 8. Order history, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders?page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 9. Sign in as the Admin
# @name admin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@orderflow.example", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 10. Staff view of every order
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/orders?page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 11. Messages that used all their retries, and the audit log
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/failed-messages
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/audit-logs?page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 12. Readiness: SQL Server, Redis, and Kafka. Stop Redis and it reports Degraded while the API keeps serving
GET http://localhost:53375/health/ready
